// Object-Oriented Programming - It is a programming approach which revolves around objects
// Object - Any entity in the system that can be defined as a set of properties using the entities property
// set is known as object .

// 5 Key principles : Encapsulation , Data Hiding , Inheritance , Polymorphism , Abstraction .

// Classes and objects : 
// 1. Class is a blueprint of an object . 
// 2. Class is a description of Objects property set and set of operations 
// 3. Creating class is as good as defining a new data type .
// 4. Class is a means to achieve encapsulation .
// 5. Object is a runtime entity  .
// 6. Object is an instance (example) of a class .

// This keyword - It refers to the current object
// the specific object whose method or constructor is currently executing .
// Using this.name explicitly tells java compiler "I mean the instance variable of this object not the parameter."
// public void set_data(String name , String color , int gears , int price){
           this.name = name;
           this.color = color;
           this.gears = gears;
           this.price = price; }

// Construction -
// 1. It is a member function of a class
// 2. It has the same name as name of the class
// 3. It has no return type , so cannot use return keyword
// 4. It must be an instance member function that is it can never be static

// How to call constructor
// 1. Constructor is implicitly invoked just after the creation of an object
// 2. Constructor is used to solve the problem of Initialization

